ValidateManifest enforces the three-way contract: NUM_FEATURES, manifest.num_features, and the length returned by BuildFeaturesAt() must match before OnInit succeeds. This exists because the failure mode it prevents is silent and expensive: add a ninth feature to FeatureBuilder.mqh without updating the deployed manifest, and without this check the EA would happily keep running with a reference window built against the old 8-feature shape while the live window silently carries 9 — the drift score would still produce a number, it would just be meaningless rather than throwing an obvious error.
